// Title: Potential DCOM InternetExplorer.Application DLL Hijack
// Sigma ID: 2f7979ae-f82b-45af-ac1d-2b10e93b0baa
// Status: test | Level: critical
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez @Cyb3rWard0g, Open Threat Research (OTR), wagga
// Date: 2020-10-12 | Modified: 2022-12-18
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, T1021.002, T1021.003
// Description: Detects potential DLL hijack of "iertutil.dll" found in the DCOM InternetExplorer.Application
//   Class over the network
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://threathunterplaybook.com/hunts/windows/201009-RemoteDCOMIErtUtilDLLHijack/notebook.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_dcom_iertutil_dll_hijack.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath =~ "System" and FolderPath endswith "\\Internet Explorer\\iertutil.dll"
